# The committed fingerprint-index.json holds SHA-256 digests of the files under
# tree/, so those bytes have to be identical in every checkout. This repository
# is cloned on Windows too, where core.autocrlf rewrites line endings on
# checkout, which would change every digest and silently stop the index from
# matching anything. Telling git these paths are not text is what keeps the
# golden snapshot reproducible across platforms.
#
# This is the same gap the matcher documents and declines to paper over: it
# hashes raw bytes so an operator can verify a claim with sha256sum, and
# line-ending tolerance belongs in the corpus builder as extra entries, not in
# the comparison.
* -text
